# ── npm-internal packages in node:22-alpine ───────────────────────────────────
#
# The following CVEs affect packages that are bundled inside npm's own private
# node_modules directory (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/).
# They are NOT application dependencies and cannot be upgraded by the project.
# Remediation requires a Node.js/npm base-image update that ships patched
# bundled versions. All are confirmed npm-internal via container inspection.
# Owner: repo maintainer | Review: 2027-04
#
# brace-expansion (v5.0.9 in npm bundled by node:22-alpine with npm@latest)
# DoS via crafted glob patterns. Not reachable through application code paths.
# Fixed in brace-expansion 5.0.10+ — awaiting npm release that bundles it.
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
#
# brace-expansion (v2.0.2 in npm bundled by node:22-alpine default npm)
# Same DoS class of vulnerability in the 1.x/2.x branch.
# Fixed in brace-expansion 2.1.2+ — awaiting npm release that bundles it.
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
#
# compression (v1.8.1) — npm-internal; memory-leak DoS. Fixed in 1.8.2.
CVE-2026-87776
#
# ip-address (v10.1.0) — npm-internal; inconsistent IP parsing. Fixed in 10.3.1.
CVE-2026-69192
#
# pacote (v19.0.2) — npm-internal package fetcher; DoS via crafted rawSpec. Fixed in 21.5.1.
CVE-2026-9496
#
# picomatch (v4.0.3) — npm-internal; ReDoS. Fixed in 4.0.4.
CVE-2026-33671
#
# sigstore (v3.1.0) — npm-internal provenance client; unauthorised cert acceptance. Fixed in 4.1.1.
CVE-2026-48815
#
# http-cache-semantics (v4.2.0) — npm-internal HTTP cache policy library.
# Not present in any service package-lock.json; confirmed npm-internal via lock-file inspection.
# Information disclosure via max-stale Cache-Control directive. No fixed version available.
CVE-2026-93748

# ── Application dependency overrides — all backend services ──────────────────
#
# braces v3.0.3 — pinned via npm "overrides" in all six backend service package.json
